{
  "Package": "Pirat",
  "Type": "Package",
  "Title": "Precursor or Peptide Imputation under Random Truncation",
  "Description": "Pirat enables the imputation of missing values (either\nMNARs or MCARs) in bottom-up LC-MS/MS proteomics data using a\npenalized maximum likelihood strategy. It does not require any\nparameter tuning, it models the instrument censorship from the\ndata available. It accounts for sibling peptides correlations\nand it can leverage complementary transcriptomics measurements.",
